Lettings Village — Dwelly hackathon demonstration

The four bundled replays and synthetic world records derive from the local
lettings-ops-agent project, licensed under Apache License 2.0. A copy of that
license is provided in LICENSE-THIRD-PARTY. Sources are recorded in each JSONL
opening event, together with SHA-256 hashes of the original state and trace.
The replays are transformed and presentation timing is compressed. Original
trace timestamps remain in recorded_at. Personal and company records are
synthetic, as declared by the source mock-world data.

The original baseline recordings each contain one real model decision. They
are not multi-turn golden episodes. They predate the stage/definition-of-done
fields, so those fields remain explicitly unrecorded. The fraud recording
contains proactive refusals by the model, not policy-gate deny invocations.

Original procedural village artwork is dedicated under CC0-1.0. No commercial
game sprites, third-party fonts or external image assets are included.

The public scenario evidence in demo/web/public-scenarios.json is adapted from
DwellyOrg/HackatonPublicCases, Property Management cases 017, 021 and 025,
revision 9bcdca585955dfb930005ed742572606e68f5688. Original source links and
SHA-256 hashes accompany each case. These source cases are synthetic.
The village mapping, participant choices, simulated dialogue, relative timing
and success checks are demo adaptations, not recorded LLM runs or evaluations.
